I was just playing (what I thought was) a very careful orcish rogue.
I levelled up my pet faster than I leveled myself, I tamed all animals
that I could, I avoided the mines for fear of being surrounded or
killed by a wand, and I went for Sokoban to hopefully acquire
reflection.

I opened the door to the chamber on the second Sokoban level and sent
in my large dog first.  I had to shuffle a bit because I wanted to
tame a pony that I knew was inside and a hostile dwarf entered the
hallway armed with a wand of lightning.  His first zap left me at 10
hp and little hope since I was so far away from him or from a corner
to hide behind.  I had two apparent options: zap my wand of magic
missile (my only useful wand), or read a scroll of earth.  I hit the
dwarf with 3 missiles (2 zaps and 1 bounce) but he hit me the next
turn and it was DYWYPI.  The scroll of earth might have been the
better choice since blessed would not have hit me, uncursed would have
hit me for d20 (IIRC) but cursed would have hit me for d20 and left me
exposed.

This death was preventable since I should have expected a wand wielder
in the room having not found the level's wand yet.  However, do people
who pull off ascension streaks really play this carefully?  Would many
people playing normally have survived this?

